{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01287",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 8.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "I mean, uh, hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.59,
      "end_seconds": 14.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.63,
      "end_seconds": 20.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.67,
      "end_seconds": 33.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "Okay, so it's a lump feeling in the throat, mostly. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.57,
      "end_seconds": 37.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.4,
      "end_seconds": 52.35,
      "duration_seconds": 13.95,
      "text": "Let me think, I've had it since Friday. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I've also had a cough at night, since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.99,
      "end_seconds": 63.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.92,
      "end_seconds": 90.38,
      "duration_seconds": 25.46,
      "text": "Maybe a six out of ten on a bad day. It just comes and goes. I did try to ignore it for a while. Oh, and food coming back up. That's been about the same, about four days. And chest discomfort after eating, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.61,
      "end_seconds": 99.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.1,
      "end_seconds": 107.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Right, it feels severe to me. Only antacids, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.72,
      "end_seconds": 112.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Have you had any black stools or anaemia?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.74,
      "end_seconds": 119.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Oh, no black stools or anaemia, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.33,
      "end_seconds": 123.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "And vomiting blood, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.87,
      "end_seconds": 130.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Let me think, uh, not at all, no vomiting blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.96,
      "end_seconds": 137.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "A few quick ones: pain on exertion, weight loss or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.48,
      "end_seconds": 147.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "Um, no, no pain on exertion, weight loss or trouble swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.25,
      "end_seconds": 151.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.79,
      "end_seconds": 155.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Ah, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.54,
      "end_seconds": 168.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.01,
      "end_seconds": 175.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Well, um, just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.02,
      "end_seconds": 179.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.42,
      "end_seconds": 191.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.29,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.53,
      "end_seconds": 196.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.95,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster diclofenac gave me wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.02,
      "end_seconds": 206.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.57,
      "end_seconds": 216.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "I'm on Foracort inhaler, twice a day. Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 218.34,
      "end_seconds": 231.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.24,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, doctor, I think the last prescription for the omeprazole was 10 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.19,
      "end_seconds": 237.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.94,
      "end_seconds": 251.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "Um, not with me. I'll bring it next time. Okay, so I take losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 253.01,
      "end_seconds": 263.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.76,
      "text": "Let me think, um, she is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.58,
      "end_seconds": 269.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "It's Eno, when I get it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.91,
      "end_seconds": 287.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.47,
      "end_seconds": 290.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I, I have asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.6,
      "end_seconds": 292.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.88,
      "end_seconds": 306.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.56,
      "text": "Well, uh, I've got acid reflux. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. High blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.82,
      "end_seconds": 314.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 316.51,
      "end_seconds": 326.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 115 over 72, temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse 76, oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.29,
      "end_seconds": 329.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.68,
      "end_seconds": 335.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.65,
      "end_seconds": 339.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.73,
      "end_seconds": 358.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Tummy is soft and non-tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.58,
      "end_seconds": 374.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards gastro-oesophageal reflux. A heart cause that we should rule out is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.8,
      "end_seconds": 378.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.04,
      "end_seconds": 387.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with gastro-oesophageal reflux do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.68,
      "end_seconds": 432.18,
      "duration_seconds": 31.5,
      "text": "Let's book an upper endoscopy to look into persistent reflux. I'd like to arrange an ECG for chest discomfort. Smaller dinners, earlier in the evening, and prop up the head of the bed with a couple of extra pillows. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Book a review in six weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 434.2,
      "end_seconds": 437.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Um, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.65,
      "end_seconds": 439.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}